[{"type":"text","value":"value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event payload value"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/EmitCustomEventOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EmitCustomEventOptions"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ batch: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep this event in the\ndurability batch instead of flushing it immediately"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const tool = toolDefinition({ ... }).server(async (args, context) => {\n  context?.emitCustomEvent('progress', { step: 1, total: 3 })\n  // ... do work ...\n  context?.emitCustomEvent('progress', { step: 2, total: 3 })\n  // ... do more work ...\n  return result\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"inputresponse","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inputResponse?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional inputResponse?: ToolInputResponse;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The answer to the input request that this tool call raised in the\nprevious run. It is set only when the run resumes an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcp_input"},{"type":"text","value":"\ninterrupt for this tool call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toolcallid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"toolCallId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional toolCallId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ID of the tool call being executed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tcontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TContext"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-declaration","text":"Type Declaration","level":2},{"id":"abortsignal","text":"abortSignal?","level":3},{"id":"emitcustomevent","text":"emitCustomEvent","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"eventname","text":"eventName","level":5},{"id":"value","text":"value","level":5},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":5},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"inputresponse","text":"inputResponse?","level":3},{"id":"toolcallid","text":"toolCallId?","level":3},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tcontext","text":"TContext","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype ToolExecutionContext<TContext> = RuntimeContextField<TContext> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:769](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L769)\n\nContext passed to tool execute functions, providing capabilities like\nemitting custom events during execution.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### abortSignal?\n\n```ts\noptional abortSignal?: AbortSignal;\n```\n\nAbort signal for the current chat run. Aborts when the run's\n`abortController` fires (or middleware aborts). Long-running tools —\ne.g. MCP `callTool` — should forward this to cancel in-flight work.\n\n### emitCustomEvent\n\n```ts\nemitCustomEvent: (eventName, value, options?) => void;\n```\n\nEmit a custom event during tool execution.\nEvents are streamed to the client in real-time as AG-UI CUSTOM events.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### eventName\n\n`string`\n\nName of the custom event\n\n##### value\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `any`\\>\n\nEvent payload value\n\n##### options?\n\n[`EmitCustomEventOptions`](../interfaces/EmitCustomEventOptions.md)\n\nPass `{ batch: true }` to keep this event in the\n  durability batch instead of flushing it immediately\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst tool = toolDefinition({ ... }).server(async (args, context) => {\n  context?.emitCustomEvent('progress', { step: 1, total: 3 })\n  // ... do work ...\n  context?.emitCustomEvent('progress', { step: 2, total: 3 })\n  // ... do more work ...\n  return result\n})\n```\n\n### inputResponse?\n\n```ts\noptional inputResponse?: ToolInputResponse;\n```\n\nThe answer to the input request that this tool call raised in the\nprevious run. It is set only when the run resumes an `mcp_input`\ninterrupt for this tool call.\n\n### toolCallId?\n\n```ts\noptional toolCallId?: string;\n```\n\nThe ID of the tool call being executed\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` = `unknown`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ToolExecutionContext\ntitle: ToolExecutionContext\n---\n\n```ts\ntype ToolExecutionContext<TContext> = RuntimeContextField<TContext> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:769](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L769)\n\nContext passed to tool execute functions, providing capabilities like\nemitting custom events during execution.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### abortSignal?\n\n```ts\noptional abortSignal?: AbortSignal;\n```\n\nAbort signal for the current chat run. Aborts when the run's\n`abortController` fires (or middleware aborts). Long-running tools —\ne.g. MCP `callTool` — should forward this to cancel in-flight work.\n\n### emitCustomEvent\n\n```ts\nemitCustomEvent: (eventName, value, options?) => void;\n```\n\nEmit a custom event during tool execution.\nEvents are streamed to the client in real-time as AG-UI CUSTOM events.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### eventName\n\n`string`\n\nName of the custom event\n\n##### value\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `any`\\>\n\nEvent payload value\n\n##### options?\n\n[`EmitCustomEventOptions`](../interfaces/EmitCustomEventOptions.md)\n\nPass `{ batch: true }` to keep this event in the\n  durability batch instead of flushing it immediately\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst tool = toolDefinition({ ... }).server(async (args, context) => {\n  context?.emitCustomEvent('progress', { step: 1, total: 3 })\n  // ... do work ...\n  context?.emitCustomEvent('progress', { step: 2, total: 3 })\n  // ... do more work ...\n  return result\n})\n```\n\n### inputResponse?\n\n```ts\noptional inputResponse?: ToolInputResponse;\n```\n\nThe answer to the input request that this tool call raised in the\nprevious run. It is set only when the run resumes an `mcp_input`\ninterrupt for this tool call.\n\n### toolCallId?\n\n```ts\noptional toolCallId?: string;\n```\n\nThe ID of the tool call being executed\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` = `unknown`\n"}
